  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Crankshaft
  description: The Crankshaft is a large, complex-shaped component located at the
    middle-center-center of the rocket engine, constructed from a material that provides
    the necessary strength and durability. Its primary function is to convert the
    reciprocating motion of the engine's pistons into rotary motion, which is then
    transmitted to the engine's output shaft. An interesting detail about the Crankshaft
    is that its design must accommodate the high stresses and loads imposed by the
    engine's combustion process, while also providing a stable and durable connection
    to the engine's transmission system.
